  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat overtime multiplier applies to Mark's weekend work? Mark used to make $11 per hour.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Overtime is commonly paid at **time-and-a-half**.\n2. Therefore, the multiplier is \\(1.5\\).\n3. At Mark’s former rate, that would be \\(11 \\times 1.5=\\$16.50\\) per hour.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1.5\\times\\text{ (time-and-a-half)}}\n\\]\n\n(Unless Mark’s employer has a different weekend-overtime policy.)",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"Solve this problem step by step. Put you\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Mark used to make $10 per hour.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. The overtime multiplier is still **time-and-a-half**, or \\(1.5\\).\n2. Mark’s overtime rate is:\n   \\[\n   \\$10 \\times 1.5 = \\$15\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1.5\\times\\text{, or } \\$15\\text{ per hour}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How much would Mark earn for an 8-hour regular workday? Additionally, Mark works 8 regular hours in a standard weekday shift.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Mark’s regular hourly wage is \\(\\$10\\).\n2. He works \\(8\\) regular hours:\n   \\[\n   8 \\times \\$10 = \\$80\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$80}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Mark works 8 hours a day for 6 days a week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Assuming overtime begins after **40 hours per week**:\n\n1. Total weekly hours:\n   \\[\n   8 \\times 6 = 48\\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n2. Regular pay for 40 hours:\n   \\[\n   40 \\times \\$10 = \\$400\n   \\]\n\n3. Overtime hours:\n   \\[\n   48 - 40 = 8\\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n4. Overtime rate:\n   \\[\n   \\$10 \\times 1.5 = \\$15\\text{/hour}\n   \\]\n\n5. Overtime pay:\n   \\[\n   8 \\times \\$15 = \\$120\n   \\]\n\n6. Total weekly earnings:\n   \\[\n   \\$400+\\$120=\\boxed{\\$520}\n   \\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How much money does Mark make in one week? One more thing you should know: Mark's pay was raised by $2 per hour.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Mark’s new hourly wage is:\n   \\[\n   \\$10+\\$2=\\$12\\text{/hour}\n   \\]\n\n2. He works:\n   \\[\n   8\\times 6=48\\text{ hours per week}\n   \\]\n\n3. Assuming overtime begins after 40 hours, he works \\(8\\) overtime hours.\n\n4. Regular pay:\n   \\[\n   40\\times \\$12=\\$480\n   \\]\n\n5. Overtime rate:\n   \\[\n   \\$12\\times 1.5=\\$18\\text{/hour}\n   \\]\n\n6. Overtime pay:\n   \\[\n   8\\times \\$18=\\$144\n   \\]\n\n7. Total weekly pay:\n   \\[\n   \\$480+\\$144=\\boxed{\\$624}\n   \\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Mark's employer pays 1.5 times the regular hourly rate for weekend work.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark’s new regular wage is:\n\n\\[\n\\$10+\\$2=\\$12\\text{/hour}\n\\]\n\nAssuming he works **5 weekdays and 1 weekend day**:\n\n- Weekday pay:  \n  \\[\n  5\\times 8\\times \\$12=\\$480\n  \\]\n\n- Weekend overtime rate:  \n  \\[\n  1.5\\times \\$12=\\$18\\text{/hour}\n  \\]\n\n- Weekend pay:  \n  \\[\n  8\\times \\$18=\\$144\n  \\]\n\nTherefore, Mark earns:\n\n\\[\n\\$480+\\$144=\\boxed{\\$624\\text{ per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Mark works 8 hours a day for 5 days a week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark’s new regular wage is:\n\n\\[\n\\$10+\\$2=\\$12\\text{ per hour}\n\\]\n\nHe works:\n\n\\[\n8\\times 5=40\\text{ hours per week}\n\\]\n\nSince 40 hours is the regular workweek, there is no overtime. Therefore:\n\n\\[\n40\\times \\$12=\\boxed{\\$480\\text{ per week}}\n\\]\n\nThis assumes all five workdays are regular weekdays.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
